[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4060128853","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117411#issuecomment-4060128853","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117411","id":4060128853,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7yAKZV","user":{"login":"TrueJole","id":121569485,"node_id":"U_kgDOBz8AzQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121569485?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole","html_url":"https://github.com/TrueJole","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrueJole/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-14T09:12:08Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T09:12:08Z","body":"I am not as experienced with shaders, but I will try my best. \nI believe this is the intended behaviour. It has nothing to do with global uniforms, you can remove them completely. The \"problem\" is accessing `POSITION` when you likely meant `VERTEX`. \nAs the docs say, `POSITION` _can_ be overwritten, which is likely what happened in your code, even though you only wanted to read from it. But because you didn't actually write anything useful to `POSITION`, the material is rendered black.\nSee [docs](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.6/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/spatial_shader.html#doc-spatial-shader):\n\n> Users can override the modelview and projection transforms using the POSITION built-in. If POSITION is written to anywhere in the shader, it will always be used, so the user becomes responsible for ensuring that it always has an acceptable value. When POSITION is used, the value from VERTEX is ignored and projection does not happen. However, the value passed to the fragment shader still comes from VERTEX.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4060128853/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4064832512","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117411#issuecomment-4064832512","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117411","id":4064832512,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ySGwA","user":{"login":"CsloudX","id":35988767,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1OTg4NzY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35988767?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX","html_url":"https://github.com/CsloudX","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-16T03:31:53Z","updated_at":"2026-03-16T03:31:53Z","body":"YES, this issue's test code maybe wrong, so i will close 